2. Documentation content about the libraries
--------------------------------------------

Prose and structured data that describe the StangaNetLib libraries
(API summaries, examples embedded for illustration, library overviews,
and similar documentation content) are provided for reference only.

That content is not licensed under the MIT grant above. It refers to,
and remains subject to, the license of each corresponding library:

  - Prefer the LICENSE (or equivalent) file in the library’s own
    repository under https://github.com/StangaNet
  - If a library has no explicit license file, the applicable terms
    are those of the StangaNet organization defaults and any license
    stated on the organization’s or repository’s GitHub pages

In particular, StangaNet library source code is typically distributed
under the “StangaNet Source-Available License” (or a successor). Viewing
this documentation does not grant rights beyond those licenses. Names,
signatures, and behavior of APIs remain the intellectual property of
their respective owners under those terms.

Do not assume that MIT (or any other permissive license) applies to the
library packages, their source, or non-structural documentation excerpts
that merely describe them.


3. Third-party components
-------------------------

Dependencies declared in package.json (React, Vite, Tailwind, and other
npm packages) remain under their own licenses. Fonts and any other
third-party assets are subject to their respective licenses.


4. Summary
----------

  Site structure / tooling  →  MIT (this file, section 1)
  Library docs content      →  Each library’s / org’s license (section 2)
  npm and other third parties → Their own licenses (section 3)

For questions about library licensing, see the LICENSE files in the
individual repositories at https://github.com/StangaNet
